+++ b/src/vulkan/wsi/enhance/third_party/README.md
@@ -1,9 +1,23 @@
 # Vendored shader sources
 
-Used by the Win32 WSI's upscaling (`../enh_easu.comp`, `../enh_rcas.comp`).
-Each directory has its license; the files are byte-for-byte the upstream
-ones.
+Used by the Win32 WSI's upscaling (`../enh_*.comp`). Each directory has its
+licence; the files are byte-for-byte the upstream ones.
 
-| Directory | What | License | Upstream |
+| Directory | What | Licence | Upstream |
 |---|---|---|---|
 | `fsr1/` | `ffx_a.h`, `ffx_fsr1.h`: AMD FidelityFX Super Resolution 1 (EASU, RCAS), v1.20210629 | MIT | github.com/GPUOpen-Effects/FidelityFX-FSR, `ffx-fsr/` |
+| `cas/` | `ffx_cas.h`: AMD FidelityFX Contrast Adaptive Sharpening, 1.20190610 | MIT | github.com/GPUOpen-Effects/FidelityFX-CAS, `ffx-cas/` |
+| `nis/` | `NIS_Scaler.h`, `NIS_Config.h`: NVIDIA Image Scaling SDK v1.0.3 | MIT | github.com/NVIDIAGameWorks/NVIDIAImageScaling, `NIS/` |
+| `sgsr/` | `sgsr1_shader_mobile_edge_direction.frag`: Snapdragon Game Super Resolution 1 | BSD-3-Clause | github.com/SnapdragonStudios/snapdragon-gsr, `sgsr/v1/include/glsl/`, commit d926f07 |
+| `xbr/` | `xbr-lv2-standalone.slang`: Hyllian's xBR-lv2 | MIT (in the file's header; `LICENSE.txt` repeats it) | github.com/libretro/slang-shaders, `edge-smoothing/xbr/shaders/`, commit 259ff81 |
+
+How they are used:
+
+- FSR 1 and CAS are included as they are (`A_GPU`, `A_GLSL`).
+- NIS's GLSL path is included as it is; its coefficient tables are
+  generated from `NIS_Config.h` at build time (`../adapt.py nis-coef`) as
+  constant arrays the shader reads instead of textures.
+- SGSR 1 and xBR-lv2 are fragment shaders; `../adapt.py` turns a copy of
+  each into a function a compute shader calls (it removes the `#version`,
+  the stage inputs and outputs and the resource declarations, and renames
+  `main`), at build time. The vendored files stay unmodified.
